# 10 — Method Argument Limits

Functions and methods should have at most 6 named parameters and must never have more than 10.

When a signature would need more than 6, split the work into smaller, well-organized helper functions, or group related parameters into a parameter object. A parameter object counts as one parameter. It must follow the other rules too, including an orienting comment on its type and each of its fields.
